{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1397578-real-world-vampire-scares-reports-for-your-chronicle","id":1397578,"title":"Real World Vampire Scares/Reports for your chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-19T14:18:47-07:00","id":1397578,"title":"Real World Vampire Scares/Reports for your chronicle","content":"One of the things I liked about early edition Vampire is that they made a concerted effort for the setting to reflect the real world. By which I mean they took real world events and showed how they were either exploited by Vampires, or showed Vampire activity behind the scenes. It was occasionally taken too far when it seemed like every famous person had become a vampire, or when it implied vampires caused everything to happen. But that can be ignored. For example, I think Chicago By Night benefited tremendously by the care in which many of the city's NPCs were part of its living history, and had gone through events as mortals or vampires that reflected the city as it was in the past. Many future city by night books did not take that approach, and I think they suffered for them - they were generic vampires (very often clearly someone's PC or PC group) in generic cities as opposed to characters that seemed part of the city.<br /> <br /> In its general setting, the writers also took care to mention how big world events were used by vampires. That the wars of the 17th century were used as a cover by the Camarilla to eliminate the Sabbat from most of Europe was something I thought was clever and made good use. And that the Black Death's killing of one-third to one-half of Europe's population was an impetus to the Anarch Revolt was also something I liked.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I've always been surprised that the game did not make use of two very famous vampire scares in real world history.<br /> <br /> The first was the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire#Eighteenth_century_vampire_controversy\" target=\"_blank\">18th Century Vampire Controversy</a>.<br /> <br /> The second was the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_England_vampire_panic\" target=\"_blank\">New England Vampire Panic</a> of the 19th century. While I have not read Dark Colony closely in years, I don't remember it being mentioned even then.<br /> <br /> Then there are &quot;real&quot; vampire stories like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croglin_Grange\" target=\"_blank\">vampire of Croglin Grange</a> (which I first read about in The Enchanted World volume: Night Creatures).<br /> <br /> I think these and similar real world vampire scares/reports could have been well used for some interesting history in the game, and something that could have been used in NPC backgrounds.<br /> <br /> I try to incorporate these stories into my own chronicles so wanted to share them with the board. I'm sure many of you already know about them, but others don't. If people know of other real events that were supposed to have happened (not those found in obvious fiction), please share them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T15:05:23-07:00","id":1397583,"title":"","content":"This is one of those classic cases that since revised toned down the references to vampires interacting with the real world or controlling society (cough Himmler cough), this discussion has taken place largely around Mage the most with the other gamelines still nursing a black eye over it.<br /> <br /> By that 'discussion' I mean the debate over people's preferences, and this is very much a matter of personal preferences, as to how one/the setting should set the dial of the Supernatural Setting Influencing Reality or Reality Influencing the Supernatural Setting. The classic matter that gets boiled down to ideas like: did the Order of Hermes invent High Ritual Magick and humanity thought it was cool or did humans come up with it and some of those became mages who shared it with their Mage friends who thought it was cool.<br /> <br /> Anyway, meta-commentary about how every writer, player, and group needs to determine where there preferred settings of the dials are, I'm interested to see a look at this discussion through the perspective of vampire.<br /> <br /> I definitely think that considering how the vampires of the VtM setting would react to these incidents and whether or not they played a part in them as important a question to consider as &quot;How much did vampires effect Bram Stoker or Joss Whedon, if at all?&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as a cursory examination, even if these don't reflect masquerade breaches (which is a natural option), I can still imagine that incidents like this would create panics in vampiric society. I can imagine scrambles to discover who caused the breach as vampires desperately try to cover-up or downplay the incidents.<br /> <br /> Particularly in these time periods, elders and ancilla have a decent chance of remembering the horrors of The Burning Times and any good neonate has had the Fear of the Inquisition branded into them. Each one of these incidents serves to reinforce the idea that a single mistake could mobilize humanity into frenzied bands of hunters armed with torches and stakes, but worst of all, active during the daytime.<br /> <br /> It's something I think will be really interesting to dig into and also to see what people think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T17:10:21-07:00","id":1397595,"title":"","content":"I think this is a very different situation. This is not inventing a connection to vampires that doesn't exist, and attributing actual human actions/causes to fictional vampires. Nor is it about discussing whether or how fictional stories about vampires were based on vampires in the game's setting.<br /> <br /> This about using actual references to vampires in history, and wondering what vampires did during this time and place.<br /> <br /> If the 18th century is filled with references of vampire sightings, how can you NOT use this in the game? You don't even need to address whether the corpse of Petar Blagojevich is a vampire. You can create your own cases that happened during this hysteria.<br /> <br /> So what caused it? What should be happening during this time? Is it a last gasp of the Sabbat in Eastern Europe? Did the Society of Leopold renovate itself and launch a mass attack while at the same time trying to destroy the Masquerade by providing evidence? Was it a result of Giovanni hunting down remaining Cappadocians? Was there a mysterious and sudden coincidence of torpored vampires waking up at the same time?<br /> <br /> There is a lot a Storyteller could do. It is a great un-utilized storytelling tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T18:27:58-07:00","id":1397601,"title":"","content":"One complication to using pre-1900 &quot;vampires&quot; in VtM is that vampire folklore from that period looks more like an account of Risen than Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T18:37:56-07:00","id":1397602,"title":"","content":"That's not a problem. It is no more of an obstacle than using vampires in the Modern Age or the Dark Ages setting. Who cares that folkloric vampires are likely mapped to a variety of creatures in the WoD - VtM vampires, fomori, spectres, risen, or whatever? If that is a problem, then you simply can't use VtM vampires at all.<br /> <br /> Besides, folklore isn't going to report incidents of vampirism perfectly. It'll be flawed eye witness reports interpreting things imperfectly. Of course it'll get many things wrong. It doesn't present any obstacles to using it as inspiration to do something interesting in that time period and place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-19T21:00:55-07:00","id":1397621,"title":"","content":"Looking at how vampires might have interacted with these sorts of cases specifically, I think there are a few sorts of categories that occur to me the most.<br /> <br /> I feel the most obvious option is that these are the results of masquerade breaches. A few unlucky or ignorant vampires active in these areas draw attention, bungle an attack, seek help aimlessly, or fall victim to the masquerade (as the flaw may suggest) and they draw the attention of humanity. The communities go into uproar, hunt down vampires viciously, and the vampiric communities go to ground as hunters flock to the area. <br /> <br /> The second notion that occurs to me is that these could be instances of intentional masquerade breaches. Whether part of Sabbat crusades or what have you, the masquerade was tactically broken or combat slipped out of hand, the attention of the locals were caught and what follows is similar to the previous option.<br /> <br /> The third option that strikes me and the one that might make for an interesting twist to a chronicle is that there were no vampires involved. These incidents were caused by mundane misunderstanding and superstition and led to 'ordinary' hysteria. This same hysteria is reflected by the vampires who turn on each other viciously as they tried to find the breach and pacify the mortals without drawing further attention to themselves.<br /> <br /> I can also see a chronicle itself being focused on the vampires tasked with covering up these incidents. I can imagine fierce debates in elysium between elders wanting to throw scapegoats to the hunters and others who would argue that it would only end up feeding the hunters, like the inquisition. Vampires would try to reign in the public, influence the government to limit these hunts, lead hunters astray, and produce doctored evidence for alternative explanations. Anything at all to appease this situation while some vampires would want to use hunters to purge their enemies and others would have to fend off hunters themselves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T01:00:31-07:00","id":1397635,"title":"","content":"So according to the very linked Wikipedia article talking about the 18th century controversy, there's a description of Voivode Matei Basarab (revenant?) passing laws concerning belief in vampires. And that, following the advice of Patriarch Postnicul, folk were warned against destroying the bodies of suspected vampires.<br /> <br /> Indeed, that if people dig up graves and find them covered in blood, that it's a trick by Satan, and it would be a mortal sin to disturb the bodies by staking or burning them. Instead, the people of the community should be doused in holy water at the end of a ritual, as should the suspected body.<br /> <br /> Now this could have merely been the work of a well-meaning priest, who had sincere theological problems with desecrating the dead. Or it might have been Technocrats, using their rising influence within the Church (in those days when they had it) to reinforce the power of official religious intervention (&quot;don't do it yourself, let the Church handle it; support your institutions, because they know better&quot;).<br /> <br /> But obviously, it could be that the Tzimisce used one of their puppet rulers (assuming Matei Basarab wasn't a Tzimisce vampire himself) to tamp down on vampire hunters.<br /> <br /> Sure, being splashed with holy water might not be much more healthy than getting staked or burned. But 1) not all priests have the True Faith needed to create caustic holy water (and lowering the chance is better than nothing), and 2) forcing the community to engage in a big church rite gives a sleeping vampire time to flee (or, in the case of the Tzimisce, to fleshcraft a suitable corpse replacement). Not even mentioning if the vampires in the area might make sure a priest under their control performs the ritual, so no actual holy water gets used.<br /> <br /> Also, even if the bodies dug up from graves aren't vampires, most Kindred would prefer to keep vigilante vampire hunting and public panic to a minimum. Convince them that any bodies covered in blood are &quot;merely&quot; a devil's trick, and they'll be gaslighted into doubting their own senses when they find evidence. Convince them that they don't need to rush to action, because the church will handle it, and the people will be slow to investigate or follow up on potential sightings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T11:25:06-07:00","id":1397772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1397578-real-world-vampire-scares-reports-for-your-chronicle#post1397578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there are &quot;real&quot; vampire stories like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croglin_Grange\" target=\"_blank\">vampire of Croglin Grange</a> (which I first read about in The Enchanted World volume: Night Creatures).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man! This brings back memories of reading <i>More Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark</i> in gradeschool and being absolutely terrified by &quot;The Window&quot;!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T16:41:07-07:00","id":1397842,"title":"","content":"I've featured vampire fiction a few times, with assorted Kindred accusing each other of breaking the Masquerade by allowing this book to be published or that film to be released, but I haven't drawn directly from a 'real' case. if I were, i might go for <a href=\"https://www.davidcastleton.net/gorbals-vampire-glasgow-southern-necropolis\" target=\"_blank\">the Gorbals Vampire</a> from 1950s Glasgow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T22:03:50-07:00","id":1397896,"title":"","content":"I was disheartened to learn that the chupacabra might just be someone scared from the movie Species. It's hard to think an urban legend like that was spawned by bad '90s CGI.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/earth/story/20161109-the-truth-about-a-strange-blood-sucking-monster\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cms.bbcearth.com/sites/default/files/2021-02/Homepage_search.jpeg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/earth/story/20161109-the-truth-about-a-strange-blood-sucking-monster\" target=\"_blank\"> BBC Earth | Home </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.bbc.com/earth/story/20161109-the-truth-about-a-strange-blood-sucking-monster\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.bbc.com/earth/story/20161109-the-truth-about-a-strange-blood-sucking-monster </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Welcome to BBC Earth, a place to explore the natural world through awe-inspiring documentaries, podcasts, stories and more. </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems like good material for a nosferatu or Tzimisce, though. You could always play it up as that article was a coverup for the masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T03:52:52-07:00","id":1397942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1397578-real-world-vampire-scares-reports-for-your-chronicle#post1397578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there are &quot;real&quot; vampire stories like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Croglin_Grange\" target=\"_blank\">vampire of Croglin Grange</a> (which I first read about in The Enchanted World volume: Night Creatures).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Vampire of Croglin Grange reference in <i><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/297539/England-Will-Burn?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_0_45633_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">England Will Burn</a></i> (because, why not?).<br /> <br /> The Croglin Grange story is quite interesting; the modern version of the story comes from Augustus Hare's autobiography, which implies it occurred in the late nineteenth century. Research by folklorists imply that the story's origins may be in the late seventeenth century, and were attached to an actual place, named Croglin Low Hall. Of course, folk tales have never had a particular need to be based in actual truth...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T18:07:19-07:00","id":1398093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1397578-real-world-vampire-scares-reports-for-your-chronicle?p=1397842#post1397842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've featured vampire fiction a few times, with assorted Kindred accusing each other of breaking the Masquerade by allowing this book to be published or that film to be released, but I haven't drawn directly from a 'real' case. if I were, i might go for <a href=\"https://www.davidcastleton.net/gorbals-vampire-glasgow-southern-necropolis\" target=\"_blank\">the Gorbals Vampire</a> from 1950s Glasgow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great one!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T16:34:34-07:00","id":1398456,"title":"","content":"How about the Highgate vampire in the 1970s?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T21:32:55-07:00","id":1398529,"title":"","content":"Another great pick! I wonder how many other modern vampire sightings there were in the UK?<br /> <br /> Real cases like this might need to be fictionalized in an actual chronicle to make good use of them. But I think name dropping them adds to the setting, and you can come up with interesting bits of chronicle history as a result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}